  note = {Fermionic matter sub-programme working note: fixes the numerical observable for the absolute normalisation of the angular generation split of Q14 \S6 and reports the Weil--BFS computations of it. A Baker--Campbell--Hausdorff reduction in $\mathfrak{sl}_2$ identifies the per-step $J_\Pi$-odd $J_3$ component of the metaplectic cascade generator with the oriented product $ts$ of the two shear parameters, produced by the $\mathfrak{sl}_2$ commutator $[E,F]=H$ (Q14 Proposition 6.5), not a free shear parameter. The computation uses only the $\mathfrak{sl}_2$ relations of the $\mathrm{SL}(2)$-on-$V$ model; no map from the Heisenberg bracket is supplied. The proposed observable is the accumulated oriented central-phase increment $A_c$ of the Heisenberg lift, normalised by the projected capacity $\widehat I(n)$; that $A_c$ carries the $J_3$ signal is an input of the note, not a consequence of the reduction. Under this input, at $n_3^{\mathrm{obs}}$ the normalised increment equals $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Weil}}(n_3^{\mathrm{obs}})$, to be compared with the dictionary value $\varepsilon = 1/10$ without fitting. Direct evaluation on symmetric BFS shells returns $\Theta_{\mathrm{raw}}=0$ identically; the orientation prescription is an irreducible input prior to $\mathcal{N}_A$.
 \doi{10.5281/zenodo.20601228}}
}

